  ],
  "equipment_type": "Fan coil room thermostat",
  "applies_to": "Siemens RDB160BNU AC 24 V room thermostats for 2-pipe, 2-pipe with electric heat and 4-pipe fan coil units.",
  "summary": "The RDB160BNU is an AC 24 V fan coil thermostat with BACnet MS/TP built in; it ships set to Fahrenheit (P80). Its commissioning guide prints the same 51 objects as the RDB160BN: room mode, comfort and economy setpoints, fan mode, changeover, valve outputs and setup values. MAC and device instance are set only from the thermostat's parameter menu or setup wizard.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 0,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The object table lists 'Not used' gaps (AV 7-8, AV 11, AV 17-26, BI 1, BI 4-6, BV 0, BV 6, BV 8, BV 11, MI 0); they are left out here.",
    "BV 1 and BV 2 share the printed object name 'Outputtype' (heating and cooling).",
    "MV 3 AppNr selects 2-pipe, 4-pipe or 2-pipe with electric heater; it changes the whole control application.",
    "The object table prints °C; on the RDB160BNU the display unit is set by parameter P80 (factory setting Fahrenheit), so check which unit the temperature objects report on site.",
    "Writable column taken as printed ('Yes' = W). The document does not say whether writable objects have a priority array."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "RDB160BNU Fan coil unit room thermostat with BACnet MS/TP communication - Commissioning Instructions",
    "doc_number": "A6V12045450_en--_b",
    "revision_date": "2022-06-08",
    "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/ls~MrM7S9oT7EUiMHcnrpw/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set the MS/TP MAC, device instance and baud rate at the thermostat, power-cycle it, then command the room mode with ROpMod (MV 5), the comfort setpoint with CmfSp (AV 33) and the fan with FanSpdMod (MV 2). Read ROpMode, HCSta, Fan3Spd and TR for status. There is no alarm object.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "MV 5",
        "name": "ROpMod",
        "why": "Room mode command: 1 Off, 2 Economy, 5 Comfort"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 4",
        "name": "ChoverMod",
        "why": "Heating, cooling or auto changeover"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 2",
        "name": "FanSpdMod",
        "why": "Fan off, manual speed 1-3 or auto"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 33",
        "name": "CmfSp",
        "why": "Comfort (occupied) setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 1",
        "name": "ROpMode",
        "why": "Current mode: Off, Economy or Comfort"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 2",
        "name": "HCSta",
        "why": "Currently off, heating or cooling"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 3",
        "name": "Fan3Spd",
        "why": "Current fan speed"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 0",
        "name": "TR",
        "why": "Room temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 3",
        "name": "SpTR",
        "why": "Active controller setpoint"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "ROpMod (MV 5) selects Off, Economy/Standby or Comfort from the network; value 6 hands the mode back to local control. A bus command for Off leaves only the On/Off button active on the thermostat.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "TRRemote (AV 15) is a writable remote room temperature object, and the heating/cooling changeover can be sent over BACnet (ChoverMod, MV 4). The document does not describe a timeout for network values.",
    "setup": [
      "MAC address (P58) defaults to 127; device instance defaults to 0 and is set with P59 (right 4 digits) and P60 (left 3 digits). They cannot be written over BACnet.",
      "Baud rate is set with P62: 9600, 19200, 38400 or 76800 (default).",
      "Max master is set with P61 (default 127).",
      "Address, instance and baud changes take effect only after a power cycle."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "ShdownState (BV 9) forces Off and blocks the On/Off button until it is written back to 0; it is meant for fire-alarm shutdown.",
      "LockSettings (BV 12) and BtnCnf (MV 6) lock the parameter menu and buttons; clear them if occupants report dead buttons.",
      "AppNr, valve type, fan type and dead-band objects are commissioning settings; don't write them cyclically."
    ]
  },
